A_115 - I believe vivisection is a very serious mistake, as is animal testing. We can use artificial intelligence to conduct complex research and studies; there's no need to harm living beings. In any case, we must remember that if artificial intelligence makes certain professions "less useful," we still have a duty to protect the lives of those people and find them suitable jobs. If you want to use artificial intelligence and the service is minimally costly, I recommend investing in tree planting, preferably in the United States, to avoid future repercussions due to environmental problems.